var PREMADE_LETTERS = {
  "appointment": `Date: {{letter_date}}
Ref No.: {{reference_number}}

To,
{{employee_name}}
{{employee_address}}

**Subject: Appointment as {{designation}}**

Dear {{employee_name}},

Further to your interview and subsequent discussions, we are pleased to appoint you as **{{designation}}** in the **{{department}}** department at **{{company_name}}** ("the Company"), on the following terms:

1. **Date of Joining:** {{joining_date}}
2. **Place of Work:** {{work_location}}. The Company may transfer you to any other location or client site as business needs require.
3. **Employment Type:** {{employment_type}}
4. **Compensation:** Annual CTC of \u20B9{{annual_ctc}}, with the breakup as per Annexure A. Salary is paid monthly by the {{salary_payment_day}} of the following month, subject to statutory deductions.
5. **Probation:** {{probation_months}} months from the date of joining. Confirmation is subject to satisfactory performance and is communicated in writing. The Company may extend the probation period at its discretion.
6. **Working Hours:** {{working_hours}}, Monday to Friday. {{saturday_schedule}}, with flexibility as project deadlines demand.
7. **Leave:** As per the Company Leave Policy: {{casual_leave_days}} casual leaves, {{sick_leave_days}} sick leaves and {{paid_leave_days}} paid leaves per calendar year, plus declared public holidays.
8. **Notice Period:** During probation, {{probation_notice_days}} days' written notice or salary in lieu. After confirmation, {{notice_days}} days' written notice or salary in lieu, by either party.
9. **Duties:** You will perform the duties of your role as detailed in the Scope of Work and any additional duties reasonably assigned by your reporting manager, {{manager}}.
10. **Confidentiality and IP:** You will sign the Confidentiality Agreement. All work created during your employment, including code, designs, campaigns, creatives, copy, strategies and client data, is the sole property of the Company.
11. **Conduct:** You are bound by the Company's policies, as amended from time to time, including the IT & Data Security, Social Media and Anti-Harassment policies.
12. **Outside Engagements:** You may not take up any other employment, freelance work or consultancy that conflicts with the Company's interests or its clients without prior written approval.
13. **Termination for Cause:** The Company may terminate your employment without notice for misconduct, breach of confidentiality, fraud, data theft, insubordination, or falsified documents or information.
14. **Background Verification:** This appointment is subject to satisfactory verification of your documents, references and prior employment.
15. **Governing Law:** This letter is governed by the laws of India. Courts at {{jurisdiction_city}} have exclusive jurisdiction.

Please sign and return the duplicate copy as acceptance within {{acceptance_days}} days of receipt.

We welcome you to the team.

Yours sincerely,

**{{signatory}}**
{{signatory_role}}
For **{{company_name}}**

**Acceptance:** I have read and understood the above terms and accept them.

Signature: ____________  Name: {{employee_name}}  Date: ____________

**Annexure A \u2013 Compensation Structure**

| Component | Monthly (\u20B9) | Annual (\u20B9) |
|---|---|---|
| Basic Salary | {{basic_salary_monthly}} | {{basic_salary_annual}} |
| HRA | {{hra_monthly}} | {{hra_annual}} |
| Special Allowance | {{special_allowance_monthly}} | {{special_allowance_annual}} |
| Employer PF | {{employer_pf_monthly}} | {{employer_pf_annual}} |
| Gross | {{gross_monthly}} | {{gross_annual}} |
| Performance Bonus (if any) | {{performance_bonus_if_any_monthly}} | {{performance_bonus_if_any_annual}} |
| **Total CTC** | {{total_ctc_monthly}} | {{total_ctc_annual}} |`,
  "confidentiality": `This Confidentiality Agreement ("Agreement") is made on {{letter_date}} between:

**{{company_name}}**, having its office at {{company_address}} ("the Company"), and
**{{employee_name}}**, residing at {{employee_address}} ("the Employee").

**1. Confidential Information** means all non-public information disclosed to or accessed by the Employee, in any form, including:
- client lists, contracts, pricing, proposals and campaign strategies
- ad account credentials, analytics data, reports and audience data
- source code, databases, architecture, API keys, server access and passwords
- designs, creatives, content drafts, templates and internal processes
- financial data, employee data and business plans
- any information of clients or third parties held by the Company

**2. Obligations.** The Employee shall:
- (a) keep Confidential Information strictly confidential and use it only for the Company's work;
- (b) not copy, share, upload to personal or unauthorised cloud storage, or transmit it to any third party, including through personal email, messaging apps or AI tools not approved by the Company;
- (c) not use client accounts, credentials or data for personal benefit;
- (d) follow all data-security instructions issued by the Company;
- (e) report any suspected breach or loss immediately to {{security_contact}}.

**3. Exclusions.** This Agreement does not cover information that is public through no fault of the Employee, was lawfully known to the Employee before employment, or is required to be disclosed by law (with prior notice to the Company where permitted).

**4. Intellectual Property.** All work product created by the Employee in the course of employment, including code, designs, copy, campaigns, videos and strategies, belongs exclusively to the Company. The Employee assigns all rights in such work to the Company and will not reuse or claim it as personal portfolio work without written permission.

**5. Non-Solicitation.** For {{non_solicitation_months}} months after leaving, the Employee shall not directly or indirectly solicit the Company's clients handled by the Employee, or its employees, for competing purposes.

**6. Return of Property.** On exit or on request, the Employee shall return all devices, files, documents, credentials and data, and permanently delete any copies held personally.

**7. Duration.** Obligations apply during employment and continue for {{confidentiality_years}} years after its end. Obligations regarding trade secrets and client data continue indefinitely.

**8. Remedies.** Breach may cause irreparable harm. The Company may seek injunctive relief, damages and disciplinary or legal action, in addition to any other remedy.

**9. Governing Law.** This Agreement is governed by the laws of India, with courts at {{jurisdiction_city}} having exclusive jurisdiction.

Signed by:

| For the Company | Employee |
|---|---|
| Name: {{signatory}} | Name: {{employee_name}} |
| Designation: {{signatory_role}} | Signature: ____________ |
| Signature: ____________ | Date: ____________ |
| Date: ____________ | Witness: ____________ |`,
  "joining": "Date: {{letter_date}}\nRef No.: {{reference_number}}\n\nTo,\n{{employee_name}}\n\n**Subject: Joining Details \u2013 {{designation}}**\n\nDear {{employee_name}},\n\nWelcome to **{{company_name}}**. We are delighted that you have accepted our offer. Your joining details are below.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Designation | {{designation}} |\n| Department | {{department}} |\n| Reporting To | {{manager}} |\n| Date of Joining | {{joining_date}} |\n| Reporting Time | {{reporting_time}} |\n| Reporting Location | {{reporting_location}} |\n| Point of Contact | {{hr_name}}, {{hr_phone}}, {{hr_email}} |\n\n**Day 1 schedule**\n- Reception and ID card issue\n- HR induction and document verification\n- IT setup: laptop, email, tools and access\n- Team introduction and role briefing with your manager\n\n**Please bring**\n- The signed Appointment Letter and Confidentiality Agreement\n- The documents listed in the Document Submission Request\n- One government photo ID (original) for verification\n\n**Dress code:** {{dress_code}}. **Working hours:** {{working_hours}}.\n\nIf you cannot join on the date above, please inform HR at least {{joining_change_notice_days}} days in advance. This joining is subject to successful document verification.\n\nWe look forward to a great journey together.\n\nWarm regards,\n\n**{{signatory}}**\n{{signatory_role}}\nFor **{{company_name}}**",
  "request": "Date: {{letter_date}}\n\nTo,\n{{employee_name}}\n\n**Subject: Request for Submission of Joining Documents**\n\nDear {{employee_name}},\n\nTo complete your onboarding and employee records, please submit the following documents on or before **{{submission_deadline}}** to {{hr_email}} (scanned copies) and bring the originals for verification on your date of joining.\n\n**A. Identity and Address Proof**\n1. Aadhaar Card\n2. PAN Card\n3. Passport (if available)\n4. Current address proof (utility bill / rental agreement)\n\n**B. Educational Documents**\n5. 10th and 12th mark sheets and certificates\n6. Graduation / post-graduation degree and mark sheets\n7. Professional certifications (if any)\n\n**C. Previous Employment** (if applicable)\n8. Relieving letter / experience letter from the last employer\n9. Last 3 months' salary slips\n10. Offer or appointment letter from the last employer\n11. Form 16 / previous employer's tax details\n\n**D. Banking and Statutory**\n12. Cancelled cheque or bank passbook front page\n13. UAN and PF details (if previously employed)\n\n**E. Other**\n14. 2 passport-size photographs\n15. Updated resume\n16. Emergency contact details (name, relationship, phone)\n17. Portfolio or work samples (for creative / technical roles)\n\n**Notes**\n- Documents must be clear, legible and valid.\n- Any false or misleading document may lead to withdrawal of the offer or termination of employment.\n- The Company will treat all personal information as confidential and use it only for employment purposes.\n- If any document is unavailable, please inform HR in writing before the due date.\n\nRegards,\n\n**{{signatory}}**\n{{signatory_role}}\nFor **{{company_name}}**",
  "scope": "**Employee:** {{employee_name}}\n**Designation:** {{designation}}\n**Department:** {{department}}\n**Reporting To:** {{manager}}\n**Effective Date:** {{effective_date}}\n\n**1. Purpose of Role**\nTo {{role_purpose}}.\n\n**2. Key Responsibilities** *(edit to role)*\n- Plan, execute and optimise digital campaigns across Google Ads, Meta Ads and other paid channels\n- Create and manage content calendars and social media content for client accounts\n- Manage SEO activities: keyword research, on-page and off-page optimisation, and reporting\n- Develop, maintain and test websites and landing pages (for technical roles)\n- Prepare weekly and monthly performance reports with insights and recommendations\n- Coordinate with designers, developers and account managers on timely delivery\n- Communicate with clients on deliverables, updates and feedback\n- Maintain accurate documentation, trackers and project records\n- Follow brand guidelines and quality standards on all deliverables\n- Stay current with platform updates and industry trends\n\n**3. Deliverables and KPIs**\n\n| Area | Metric | Target |\n|---|---|---|\n| Campaign performance | ROAS / CPL / CTR | {{campaign_target}} |\n| Timelines | On-time delivery rate | {{on_time_target}} |\n| Quality | Revisions per deliverable | {{revision_target}} |\n| Reporting | Reports submitted on schedule | {{reporting_target}} |\n| Client satisfaction | Feedback score | {{client_satisfaction_target}} |\n\n**4. Tools and Systems Access**\n{{tools_and_systems}}\n\n**5. Reporting and Review**\nDaily updates to {{manager}}, a weekly team meeting, and a monthly performance review. A formal appraisal follows probation and then annually.\n\n**6. Authority and Limits**\nThe Employee may not commit spend, timelines or scope changes to clients without written manager approval, and may not share access credentials outside authorised personnel.\n\n**7. Changes**\nThe Company may reasonably revise this scope based on business needs, with notice to the Employee.\n\nAcknowledged:\n\n| Manager | Employee |\n|---|---|\n| Name: {{manager}} | Name: {{employee_name}} |\n| Signature: ____________ | Signature: ____________ |\n| Date: ____________ | Date: ____________ |",
  "policy": "**Employee Name:** {{employee_name}}\n**Designation:** {{designation}}\n**Employee ID:** {{employee_id}}\n**Date of Joining:** {{joining_date}}\n\nI, {{employee_name}}, confirm that I have received, read and understood the following Company policies, and I agree to comply with them:\n\n| # | Policy | Version / Date | Initials |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Code of Conduct and Ethics | | |\n| 2 | IT and Information Security Policy | | |\n| 3 | Data Protection and Privacy Policy | | |\n| 4 | Acceptable Use of Company Devices and Internet | | |\n| 5 | Social Media Policy | | |\n| 6 | Client Confidentiality Policy | | |\n| 7 | Attendance, Leave and Working Hours Policy | | |\n| 8 | Prevention of Sexual Harassment (POSH) Policy | | |\n| 9 | Anti-Bribery and Conflict of Interest Policy | | |\n| 10 | Work From Home / Remote Work Policy | | |\n| 11 | Intellectual Property Policy | | |\n\n**I understand and agree that:**\n1. Company policies may be updated, and I will follow the latest version communicated to me.\n2. Company systems, email and devices may be monitored for security and compliance, as permitted by law.\n3. I will not use client or Company data, credentials or accounts for personal purposes.\n4. I will not post confidential, client or Company information on any public platform, and I will not represent the Company on social media without authorisation.\n5. Violation of any policy may lead to disciplinary action, up to and including termination and legal action.\n6. I will raise questions or concerns with HR at {{hr_email}}, and I know how to report violations or grievances.\n\nEmployee Signature: ____________\nDate: ____________\n\n**For HR use:** Received by: ____________  Date: ____________\n\n---"
};

